<!-- SECTION: movement.Movement — title -->
<div class="titleband" data-screen-label="Movement — title"><h1>The <span class="u-1">Movement</span></h1></div>
<div class="introband">
  <h2>From agreement to <span class="u-1">action</span> — one front door.</h2>
  <p>The Movement is how Uncost turns a widely felt frustration into organized momentum: reach people with something true and shareable, welcome them in, and offer a clear path to act. Every piece of content points back here — a place to join, learn more, or take part.</p>
</div>

<!-- SECTION: movement.How it reaches people -->
<section class="u-87 blk blk--cream" data-screen-label="How it reaches people">
  <div class="eyebrow">How it reaches people</div>
  <h2 class="u-88 sec">Short, visual, <span class="u-1">source-led</span> — never outrage alone.</h2>
  <p class="u-89 lead">Explainers, data pieces, and the movement&rsquo;s own illustrated style, distributed where attention already is — and carried further by values-aligned creators sharing with their own audiences. Public content must lead back to evidence and practical action.</p>
</section>

<!-- SECTION: movement.Engagement tools -->
<section class="blk blk--cream2" data-screen-label="Engagement tools">
  <div class="eyebrow">Three ways in</div>
  <h2 class="u-6 sec">The early engagement tools.</h2>
  <div class="tools">
    <div class="tool"><h3>The Pledge</h3><div class="st-row"><span class="u-90 status status--live">Designed — opens at launch</span></div><p>A simple public commitment to the movement&rsquo;s core principles. After signing, share it onward if you choose — that&rsquo;s how the count grows.</p><div class="go"><a href="/pledge/">Read and sign the Pledge →</a></div></div>
    <div class="tool"><h3>The cost-of-living quiz</h3><div class="st-row"><span class="status status--planned">Planned</span></div><p>&ldquo;Guess what living actually costs&rdquo; — a short interactive test that teaches something surprising, and offers the full breakdown when you join.</p><div class="go"><a href="/quiz/">What&rsquo;s planned →</a></div></div>
    <div class="tool"><h3>Share-a-stat</h3><div class="st-row"><span class="status status--planned">Planned</span></div><p>Ready-made, sourced cost-of-living facts as graphics and short videos — supporters repost them to their own networks, spreading the message for free. Only published, source-backed figures can become share assets.</p><div class="go"><a href="/share/">What&rsquo;s planned →</a></div></div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- SECTION: movement.The path -->
<section class="blk blk--ink u-block--ink" data-screen-label="The path">
  <div class="u-5 eyebrow">The path from agreement to action</div>
  <h2 class="u-91 sec">Support. Contribute. <span class="u-1">Partner.</span></h2>
  <div class="path">
    <div class="p"><h3>Support</h3><p>Free actions for anyone who agrees living costs too much: join, share sourced material, take the quiz, sign the Pledge. This builds the public demand that makes the rest possible.</p></div>
    <div class="p"><h3>Contribute</h3><p>Back the work directly — volunteer research, data, engineering, writing, design, translation, or moderation; donate once the sponsor gate opens.</p></div>
    <div class="p"><h3>Partner</h3><p>Experts, builders, institutions, and companies: build the tools, advise, coordinate a sector or region, or provide reviewed in-kind support.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="u-92">
    <a href="/join/" class="u-btn u-btn--primary">Take Part</a>
    <a href="/news/" class="u-btn u-btn--outline-cream">Follow the news</a>
  </div>
</section>

